Feature: Mask the last four digits of invoice_number in d_product_revenue_clone table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" is accessible
    And the schema "purgo_playground" exists
    And the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" does not exist
    When the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" is dropped if it exists
    And a replica of "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" is created as "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"

  Scenario: Successfully mask the last four digits of a valid invoice_number
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with invoice_number "1234234534"
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then the invoice_number for that record should be "123423****"
    And the data type of invoice_number should be "string"

  Scenario Outline: Mask multiple invoice_number values with varying formats
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with invoice_number "<original_invoice_number>"
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then the invoice_number for that record should be "<masked_invoice_number>"
    And the data type of invoice_number should be "string"

    Examples:
      | original_invoice_number | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234234534              | 123423****            |
      | 98765432101234          | 9876543210****        |
      | 55555555                | 5555****              |
      | 00001234                | 0000****              |

  Scenario: Handle invoice_number with fewer than four digits
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with invoice_number "123"
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then an error "Invoice number must have at least 4 digits to mask" should be logged

  Scenario: Handle null invoice_number
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with a null invoice_number
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then an error "Invoice number cannot be null" should be logged

  Scenario: Ensure invoice_number data type is converted to string after masking
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with invoice_number "9876543210"
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then the masked invoice_number should be "987654****"
    And the data type of invoice_number should be "string"

  Scenario: Verify that only the last four digits are masked
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with invoice_number "567890123456"
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then the invoice_number for that record should be "56789012****"
    And the first digits before the last four should remain unchanged

  Scenario: Validate that non-numeric invoice_number values are handled appropriately
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with invoice_number "ABCDEF1234"
    When the PySpark masking job is executed
    Then an error "Invoice number must be numeric" should be logged
